          "description": "An accepted species of Helmholtzia, a genus of large rhizomatous perennial herbs in the monocot family Philydraceae (Commelinales). A rhizomatous geophyte forming robust rosettes of long ensiform (sword-shaped) leaves, its native range runs from Maluku (the Moluccas) to New Guinea, growing in the wet tropical biome."
